From 6a66aa994c20b079c530741b83c26073c17caa79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Buildroot STM32F429 demo <noreply@example.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 09:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: stm32: enable optional IRQ mux clock

Some STM32 boot flows leave the SYSCFG peripheral clock disabled.  In that
case regmap writes which select the GPIO bank for an EXTI line are silently
ignored, leaving all lines routed to GPIOA.

Allow a pinctrl node to provide an irqmux clock and keep it enabled while
the pin controller can update EXTI routing.

Signed-off-by: Buildroot STM32F429 demo <noreply@example.com>
---
 drivers/pinctrl/stm32/pinctrl-stm32.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/stm32/pinctrl-stm32.c b/drivers/pinctrl/stm32/pinctrl-stm32.c
index 346a31f00131..f86b50dcbe6a 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/stm32/pinctrl-stm32.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/stm32/pinctrl-stm32.c
@@ -1429,6 +1429,12 @@ static int stm32_pctrl_dt_setup_irq(struct platform_device *pdev,
 	int offset, ret, i;
 	int mask, mask_width;
+	struct clk *irqmux_clk;
+
+	irqmux_clk = devm_clk_get_optional_enabled(dev, "irqmux");
+	if (IS_ERR(irqmux_clk))
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(irqmux_clk),
+				     "failed to enable irq mux clock\n");
 
 	pctl->regmap = syscon_regmap_lookup_by_phandle(np, "st,syscfg");
 	if (IS_ERR(pctl->regmap))
 		return PTR_ERR(pctl->regmap);
-- 
